set of morphism of sheaves of <MATH_0014>-modules.\n<STRUCT_0005> The category of sheaves of <MATH_0015>-modules\nis denoted <MATH_0016>.\n<STRUCT_0006>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:bf22d6fe3c70bcd97f2723acf5e1541412ff80e1ac0ae608e37dd91e54e90f6d", "unit_id": "tag:0077:statement"}
{"chapter": "sheaves", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0076", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{O}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{O}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{O}$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:626dae348ef786c10da0a79f032c2eb08c7b4e5fee5cc999116a54d51ba6939f", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:91a4fede5f7b2df82a7bd39e8bb2fd4d09a41a4838c3b6669a7119948566cbca", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThis definition kind of makes sense even if <MATH_0001> is just a\npresheaf of rings, although we do not know any examples where\nthis is useful, and we will avoid using the terminology\n``sheaves of <MATH_0002>-modules''\nin case <MATH_0003> is not a sheaf of rings.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:eea0f86a27bab707cbbf140eb94e928e08a5b7d5c54e567333c932f67a27ddb4", "unit_id": "tag:0076:prose-0001"}
